    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/data-analyst-i-530581-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Data Analyst I",
      "description": "Data Analyst I - 530581 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Data Analyst I - 530581 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Data Analyst I - 530581 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Engineering/Computer Science Research/Scientific Closing at: Oct 14 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $53,500 - Midpoint: $66,900 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 600101 - Athletic Director Normal Work Schedule: Varies Job Summary: The Data Analyst I gathers, audits, analyzes, and reports low- to moderate-complexity data under general supervision. Ensures data integrity. May perform ad-hoc analyses and reporting to inform decision-making, or design predictive modeling or other data mining capabilities. Additional Department Summary: Supports UA Athletics' data management and analytics efforts by building and maintaining business intelligence solutions and delivering actionable insights across ticketing, marketing, and operational areas. Assists with reporting automation, dashboard development, and analytics. Ensures data quality. Adheres to institutional security and governance policies and procedures. Collaborates with stakeholders to enhance decision-making and improve organizational performance. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher and some data analysis experience. Skills and Knowledge: Strong analytical skills and attention to detail. Ability to translate complex data into clear, narrative driven presentations that inform leadership decision making. Proficiency in Excel. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher in business, economics, statistics, mathematics, computer science, information systems, or another related field. Experience using SQL for data management. Experience using Python and/or R for data analysis. Experience using Tableau and/or comparable BI tools for data visualization. Familiarity with CRM systems, ticketing platforms, and large-scale consumer datasets. Experience with Snowflake. Experience in college athletics (internship or full-time). Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 1aae48dc Last Name (required) a4eea1f9 Email (required) f91a8367 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 681a359b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering t