    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/custodian-regular-part-time-benefits-eligible-530433-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian - Regular Part-time (Benefits eligible) - 530433 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Custodian - Regular Part-time (Benefits eligible) - 530433 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Custodian - Regular Part-time (Benefits eligible) - 530433 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Facilities/ Grounds Closing at: Sep 19 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $15.00 - Midpoint: $17.26 (Hourly N1) Department/Organization: 500002 - Bryant Conference Center Normal Work Schedule: Varies; Includes days, nights, weekends, overtime, and some holidays. Job Summary: The Custodian performs routine manual work in housekeeping and cleaning of interior spaces and immediate exterior areas. Sweeps, mops, vacuums, polishes and dusts furniture, and cleans restrooms, windows, blinds, mirrors, etc. in buildings across campus. Additional Department Summary: Must be able to work independently and prioritize assigned tasks. Sets up event rooms with equipment and furniture. Cleans event rooms and other spaces associated with events. Performs light maintenance. Secures the building as needed. Required Minimum Qualifications: Must be able to read, write, and follow verbal and written instructions. Must maintain confidentiality. Skills and Knowledge: Ability to compose, send, and receive emails. Ability to operate and use a smartphone for business purposes. Ability to work independently and prioritize assigned tasks, including setting up event rooms with equipment and furniture. Ability to lift 50-75 pounds on a consistent basis, with or without accommodation. Ability to work varied shifts, including nights, weekends and/or holidays. Preferred Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) cfbfc9e7 Last Name (required) d22aed22 Email (required) 8275f8c1 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 87b8c212 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Facilities/ Grounds Facilities/ Grounds Employment Type Regular Part-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Part-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 13b71637 Last Name (require