    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/event-planner-529940-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Event Planner",
      "description": "Event Planner - 529940 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Event Planner - 529940 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Event Planner - 529940 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Library/Research/Scientific Closing at: Sep 21 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $48,600 - Midpoint: $60,800 (Salaried E7) Department/Organization: 219101 - University Libraries Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; nights and weekends as needed. Job Summary: The Event Planner conceptualizes event theme, itinerary, etc. Develops and manages event budgets. Oversees the implementation, execution, and follow-up for events hosted on- and off-campus. Creates invitations. Selects sites. Creates seating arrangements. Negotiates with florist, caterers, event space staff, print shops, etc. Manages on-site contract staff, students, and etc. Additional Department Summary: Manages and executes events for the University Libraries. Schedules and supports events utilizing the Library facilities by external departments. Manages event budget to ensure costs stay within allocated budgets. Performs operational duties, including but are not limited to: supervising student workers, publishing and maintaining content on the website, UA’s Events calendar, managing social media accounts for upcoming events, and managing travel logistics for guest speakers. Serves as a liaison to multiple campus and library departments, performing graphic design and memorializing events with video or still photography. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of event planning or coordination experience; OR master's degree. Skills and Knowledge: Working knowledge of digital presentation applications and hardware. Working knowledge of various office production software, including Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Ability to problem-solve. Strong communication skills, both written and verbal. Strong organizational skills. Excellent attention to detail. Ability to multi­task and follow through on commitments and elements of planning events. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher in hospitality management. Experience working with catering providers and vendors. Experience with UA Procurement system (Concur). Graphic design experience. Experience with social media account management. Experience with video production and knowledge of best practices for still photography and video. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and ac