    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/building-and-laboratory-safety-manager-530566-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Building and Laboratory Safety Manager",
      "description": "Building and Laboratory Safety Manager - 530566 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Building and Laboratory Safety Manager - 530566 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Building and Laboratory Safety Manager - 530566 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Management/General Business Other Closing at: Sep 18 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $56,600 - Midpoint: $73,600 (Salaried E9) Department/Organization: 204101 - Dean's Office-Barefield College A&S Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some early mornings, evenings & weekends as needed. Job Summary: The Building and Laboratory Safety Manager monitors activities and conducts regular inspections of working spaces and labs. Supervises and guides Building Coordinators to ensure that hazards are properly mitigated, and necessary maintenance, repairs, modifications, and deliveries are properly planned and scheduled. Oversees the development, review, and implementation of college-wide safety policies and procedures. Additional Department Summary: Works closely with College leadership with regard to laboratory safety, ensuring safe operation of laboratories, training spaces, and research equipment. Conducts safety walkthrough of research labs, teaching labs, student spaces, offices, communal areas, multidisciplinary spaces, and related facilities. Coordinates and oversees the development, review, and implementation of college-wide safety procedures. Assures compliance with University of Alabama Environment Health and Safety (UA-EHS) safety policies and protocols. Interacts with faculty, staff, and students, and requires independent judgement to take immediate corrective measures when safety violations are observed. Helps faculty, and directly submits project initiation requests, work orders, and attends required meetings related to lab renovations. Works with Departments chairs and investigators to ensure compliance with Environmental Health and Safety, and facilitates appropriate use of shared equipment. Collaborates with academic programs regarding their assigned spaces. Inspects teaching labs to ensure safety and compliance. Serves as the liaison between the Barefield College of Arts and Sciences faculty/staff and EHS, and helps to develop cost-effective hazard mitigation strategies for new projects or facilities and equipment. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of experience; OR master's degree and two (2) years of experience. Skills and Knowledge: Basic knowledge and understanding of typical university research lab safety requirements. Ability to create procedures that incorporate all requirements in coordination with EHS. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Self-motivated. Working knowledge in the usage of personal computers and standard application software (Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel). Understanding and appreciation for laboratory and workplace safety. Ability to stay abreast of all safety and accreditation requirements for all the College's research, teaching, student projects, and other related labs. Preferred Qualifications: Degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, or Biological Sciences. Lab safety or lab research experience in a university setting. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept"
