    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/data-analyst-i-530543-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Data Analyst I",
      "description": "Data Analyst I - 530543 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Data Analyst I - 530543 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Data Analyst I - 530543 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Sep 18 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $53,500 - Midpoint: $66,900 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 830106 - Career Office of Internships Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Data Analyst I gathers, audits, analyzes, and reports low- to moderate-complexity data under general supervision. Ensures data integrity. May perform ad-hoc analyses and reporting to inform decision-making, or design predictive modeling or other data mining capabilities. Additional Department Summary: Serves as the lead for collecting, analyzing, reporting, and interpreting internship data for the Office of Internships. Supports data-informed decision-making by developing assessment strategies, tracking student outcomes, identifying trends, and creating reports that demonstrate the impact of internship programs. Develops and administers internship-specific surveys, evaluations, feedback mechanisms, and other assessment tools. Works with the Career Center operations team to utilize established reporting systems, dashboards, and data resources for internship-related assessment. Compiles regular and ad-hoc reports for government officials, system and University leadership, employers, and Career Center staff. Ensures that reports are clear and easily understandable. Develops and maintains Office of Internships workflows and documentation related to assessment, information collection, evaluation, and reporting. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher and some data analysis experience. Skills and Knowledge: Advanced Excel skills, including the use of pivot tables, formulas, macros, etc. Knowledge of Microsoft Office, PowerBI, Power Automate, Tableau, and Qualtrics. Ability to learn new software programs quickly. Clear verbal and written communication skills. Strong mathematical aptitude and knowledge of statistical processes. Prioritizes and executes multiple projects simultaneously. Ability to work independently and collaboratively with professional colleagues. Exercises attention to detail with a high level of accuracy without losing sight of the “big picture.” Demonstrates commitment to supporting all students. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in management information systems, operations management, library information sciences, statistics, mathematics, or other related research or analytical fields of study; OR master's degree with relevant student or academic project experience. Two (2) years of related research or analytical experience. Experience with extracting data and creating reports that are accurate and meaningful. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) e07438b5 Last Name (required) 1ab8cbf2 Email (required) 5a8fc3f7 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 124bec24 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Information Systems/Technology Support Administrative / Professional Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) cc70e8d8 Last Name (required) f9010339 Email (required) e5ae9b0a Friend's Information a6600369 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 35f2f40c Last Name (required) d64ce073 Email (required) 9c157fa4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of acco