    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/assistant-provost-undergraduate-advising-and-engagement-530538-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Provost Undergraduate Advising and Engagement",
      "description": "Assistant Provost Undergraduate Advising and Engagement - 530538 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Assistant Provost Undergraduate Advising and Engagement - 530538 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Provost Undergraduate Advising and Engagement - 530538 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Other Closing at: Oct 9 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Not Graded Department/Organization: 200023 - The Office of Undergraduate Edu Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Assistant Provost of Undergraduate Advising and Engagement provides institutional leadership in support of undergraduate advising and engagement initiatives that advance student success. Serves as a collaborative institutional resource for colleges, advancing a student-centered framework that promotes communication, consistency, innovation, and excellence in advising. Partners with the Office of the University Registrar, Faculty Senate committees, and other campus partners to promote the implementation of undergraduate academic policies and governance decisions. Advances institutional priorities related to student engagement, retention, progression, and timely degree completion. Additional Department Summary: The Office of Undergraduate Education provides institutional leadership for undergraduate academic policy, General Education, curriculum oversight, academic advising, student engagement, assessment, and student success initiatives. Working collaboratively with academic colleges, the Office of Undergraduate Education supports the University's distributed advising model through policy coordination, communication, professional development, assessment, strategic planning, and continuous improvement. This position works in partnership with college advising leaders and campus stakeholders to support consistent implementation of undergraduate academic policies, General Education requirements, curriculum changes, and advising best practices. Convenes advising leaders, cultivates a collaborative community of practice, coordinates university-wide professional development and assessment initiatives, advocates for the advising profession, and advances institutional priorities related to student engagement, retention, progression, and timely degree completion. Contributes to the strategic planning, administration, and continuous improvement of undergraduate education initiatives across the University. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and fifteen (15) years of experience; OR master's and thirteen (13) years of experience. Skills and Knowledge: Comprehensive knowledge of undergraduate curriculum, General Education requirements, and academic policies. Knowledge of the best national practices in academic advising, including NACADA principles and emerging trends in undergraduate advising and student success. Understanding of student engagement, transition, persistence, and success strategies in higher education. Strong organizational, strategic planning, facilitation, and project management skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to analyze institutional data and develop evidence-based recommendations. Ability to build collaborative relationships across academic colleges and administrative units. Knowledge of advising technologies, degree audit platforms, and data-informed student success tools. Ability to lead through collaboration, influence, consensus-building, and strategic partnership. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Higher Education, Educational Leadership, Student Affairs, or a related field. Experience leading advising, student success, or enrollment initiatives at the college or institutional level. Experience with DegreeWorks or comparable degree audit systems. Experience leading institutional initiatives and cross-functional collaborations. Experience interpreting and implementing undergraduate academic policies and curriculum requirements. Experience utilizing student information systems, degree audit platforms, advising technologies, or comparable student success systems. Active participation in NACADA or other professional organizations related to academic advising. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) b0a6c894 Last Name (required) abaf5c74 Email (required) 03922603 Select from the lists below to receive information about s