    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/title-ix-eop-investigator-i-530395-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Title IX EOP Investigator I",
      "description": "Title IX EOP Investigator I - 530395 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Title IX EOP Investigator I - 530395 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Title IX EOP Investigator I - 530395 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Closing at: Sep 16 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $56,600 - Midpoint: $73,600 (Salaried E9) Department/Organization: 500402 - Equal Opportunity & Title IX Progra Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; Must be able to respond to crisis situations during non-work hours/days. Job Summary: The Title IX EOP Investigator I performs fact-gathering and investigative functions primarily related to sexual misconduct and harassment, and protected class discrimination and harassment incidents for faculty, staff and students. Additional Department Summary: Receives, analyzes, and investigates reports of alleged violations of the University’s Title IX and Sexual Misconduct Policy, the Harassment Policy, the Equal Opportunity and Non-Discrimination Policy, the Consensual Romantic Relationships Policy, and other applicable University policies. Accurately and promptly maintains records. Communicates and collaborates with coworkers, supervisors, campus partners, and others. Provides training to the campus community. Participates in training related to applicable federal and state laws and University policies. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of Title IX experience; OR master's degree or juris doctorate. Skills and Knowledge: Effective verbal and written communication skills. Ability to interact effectively with people. Demonstrated organizational and time management skills. Ability to conduct investigations and gather evidence. Ability to remain neutral in conducting investigations. Ability to maintain sensitive and private information. Ability to work in stressful situations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with conducting investigations and gathering evidence. Experience in human resources, law, or a related field. Experience working in a higher education setting. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) a376ea99 Last Name (required) e0ea510d Email (required) 80ee2f26 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. fb9bcf0b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple o