    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/associate-provost-strategy-and-operations-530514-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Provost Strategy and Operations",
      "description": "Associate Provost Strategy and Operations - 530514 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Associate Provost Strategy and Operations - 530514 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate Provost Strategy and Operations - 530514 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Other Closing at: Oct 8 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Not Graded Department/Organization: 200001 - VP Academic Affairs Office Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Associate Provost of Strategy and Operations provides strategic leadership, operational oversight, and executive-level management for initiatives that advance the University’s academic mission and institutional priorities. Establishes project governance structures, implementation plans, timelines, performance metrics, and accountability measures. Guides new programs and pilot initiatives from concept development through implementation, evaluation, and institutionalization. Additional Department Summary: Serves as a senior executive leader within the Office for Academic Affairs (OAA) and a key member of the Provost’s leadership team. Partners with academic and administrative leaders to translate institutional strategy into measurable outcomes, ensure effective execution of major initiatives, support resource stewardship, and strengthen organizational effectiveness across Academic Affairs. Serves as the Provost’s designated representative on academic affairs matters as assigned, and provides leadership for cross-functional initiatives, organizational change, academic operations, strategic communications, financial affairs, and resource allocation. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and fifteen (15) years of experience; OR master's and thirteen (13) years of experience. Skills and Knowledge: Demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty and academic leadership. Strong project management skills, including the ability to develop project plans, manage timelines, and ensure accountability for deliverables. Ability to exercise independent judgement, handle sensitive information, and make decisions aligned with institution priorities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to build relationships and facilitate collaboration among various stakeholders. Ability to manage multiple priorities with competing time frames. Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing complex projects in central academic units with demonstrated success leading cross-institutional initiatives in a complex higher education environment. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) a7270f34 Last Name (required) b3b8a00c Email (required) 58e3ad6f Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 2fbcc56f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Other Other Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 4713ccef Last Name (required) 8f9aaa94 Email (required) 633951bd Friend's Information b770c60f Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4605ff6a Last Name (required) 4e182db8 Email (required) 939abef9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"
