    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/reach-across-alabama-program-manager-530606-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "REACH Across Alabama Program Manager",
      "description": "REACH Across Alabama Program Manager - 530606 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode REACH Across Alabama Program Manager - 530606 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search REACH Across Alabama Program Manager - 530606 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Closing at: Sep 23 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $53,500 - Midpoint: $66,900 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 200678 - CCSS-Reach Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The REACH Across Alabama Program Manager oversees the planning and development for the REACH Across Alabama program initiatives and models to prepare for the competitive AmeriCorps Operational Grant application process. Conducts statewide student assessments, develops individualized success plans, monitors academic progress, and provides coaching with the goal of providing students with opportunities to make permanent, positive connections and academic achievement. Provides comprehensive case management and student success services to an assigned caseload of Alabama REACH scholars to promote academic success, retention, persistence, graduation, and post-graduate success. Additional Department Summary: The Alabama REACH Program is a nationally recognized student success initiative serving students with lived experience in foster care, homelessness, kinship care, and other barriers to higher education. This position supports the expansion of REACH through REACH Across Alabama, a statewide planning initiative funded by an AmeriCorps Planning Grant. Collaborates with campus and community partners throughout Alabama to develop a sustainable framework that expands educational opportunity, student success, and community engagement across the state. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of student retention or engagement experience; OR master's degree and two (2) years of student retention or engagement experience. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong project management, organizational, and analytical skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Knowledge of case management and student success principles. Knowledge of program planning, strategic planning, assessment, and evaluation methodologies. Ability to analyze qualitative and quantitative data to inform decision-making and program development. Ability to build collaborative partnerships, facilitate stakeholder engagement, and work independently while collaborating effectively with a variety of campus, community, and state partners. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Higher Education, Social Work, Counseling, Public Administration, Education, or a related field and three (3) years of progressively responsible professional experience in program administration, strategic planning, higher education, social services, community engagement, or grant-funded initiatives. Experience leading grant-funded programs or strategic planning initiatives; developing, implementing, and evaluating programs; conducting community or statewide needs assessments; facilitating stakeholder engagement; building collaborative partnerships across higher education, nonprofit organizations, and public agencies; supporting underserved populations, including students with lived experience in foster care, homelessness, kinship care, first-generation status, or rural communities; providing student success services or case management in higher education; and preparing competitive grant applications, particularly AmeriCorps grants. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 0778e339 Last Name (required) 99988f47 Email (required) 4a0450ae Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. f9ad1aca Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional