    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/education-researcher-iii-project-lift-530414-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Education Researcher III",
      "description": "Education Researcher III - Project LIFT - 530414 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Education Researcher III - Project LIFT - 530414 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Education Researcher III - Project LIFT - 530414 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Research/Scientific Closing at: Sep 23 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $68,500 - Midpoint: $89,100 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 212701 - Special Education Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for remote work subject to University policy . Salaries are commensurate with education and experience of the candidate. If an applicant is selected and will request to work from a state where the University does not currently have other regular employees, that applicant may be referred to the University’s 3rd Party Employer of Record, nextSource, to serve as the official employer. Job Summary: The Education Researcher III assumes full responsibility for overall support of education research activities. Makes significant contributions to the planning and design of research and creative projects. Assists in short- and long-term planning and project goals. May assist with research and creative proposals and dissemination of project findings. Additional Department Summary: The University of Alabama, College of Education, Department of Special Education is embarking on a five-year Education Innovation and Research (EIR) Mid-Phase grant funded by the U.S. Department of Education. Project LIFT: Literacy Improvement through Focused Tutoring, is scaling Friends on the Block, an evidence-based early literacy intervention with strong evidence of efficacy for students with disabilities, to 75 primarily rural elementary schools across Alabama over three cohorts. The project supports K–2 struggling readers with and without disabilities and develops the implementation infrastructure, a program implementation guide, a train-the-trainer model, and coaching protocols needed to sustain and scale the intervention within schools and districts. This position reports directly to Principal Investigator Dr. Gregory J. Benner and serves as the project's most senior operational leader. Works in partnership with the PI, Co-PIs (Southern Methodist University and Oregon Research Institute), the Design and Implementation Research Consultant, the Data Manager, the Evaluation Team, and consortium districts to execute Project LIFT at the University of Alabama. Ensures that Project LIFT is delivered on schedule, within budget, and in compliance with university and federal requirements. Leads the Project Management Core of Project LIFT and provides executive operational oversight across the project's six working subgroups. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and ten (10) years of education or closely related research experience; OR master's degree and eight (8) years of education or closely related research experience; OR doctoral degree and five (5) years of education or closely related research experience. Post-Baccalaureate degree is highly preferred (Master’s degree or higher). Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with executive leaders, funders, school district administrators, teachers, families, and community partners. Familiarity with early literacy intervention, the science of reading, high-impact tutoring, Multi-Tiered Systems of Support (MTSS), implementation science, and/or What Works Clearinghouse evidence standards. Knowledge of the Alabama educational context, Alabama Literacy Act, Alabama Reading Initiative, and Alabama school district operations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Outlook, Teams, and shared document-management platforms such as SharePoint or Box. Ability to exercise sound judgment, work independently, prioritize competing demands, and maintain professional relationships with partners. Ability to maintain confidentiality and protect sensitive student, school, personnel, and project information. Demonstrated commitment to serving students with disabilities and students in high-need schools. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Education, Special Education, Educational Leadership, Social Sciences, Public Administration, Business Administration, or a related field and seven (7) years of relevant professional experience. Executive-level educational leadership experience as a principal, assistant superintendent, superintendent, district-level administrator, MTSS/literacy director, or senior program administrator in a school system, state agency, university, or education nonprofit. Experience leading operations for a federally funded education research grant (e.g., EIR, IES, OSEP, NIH, NSF) or foundation-funded initiative of comparable scale. Experience coordinating multi-site randomized controlled trials, implementation studies, or large-scale education initiatives in K–12 settings. Experience partnering with rural school districts, Alabama LEAs, and school-based implementation teams. Experience coordinating subawards, subcontracts, consultant agreements, IRB submissions, human subjects protection processes, or data-use agreements. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) bb202160 Last Name (required) 4f692512 Email (required) 826a9c79 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 828f6ade Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research/Scientific Research/Scientific Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 546a300f Last Name (required) 872ea9a6 Email (required) bf34b5d2 Friend's Information dfc1b91d Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2442cfcb Last Name (required) 7c203c20 Email (required) 3b32291f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the dis