      "description": "IT Project Manager III - 530671 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode IT Project Manager III - 530671 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search IT Project Manager III - 530671 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Sep 30 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $68,500 - Midpoint: $89,100 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 500001 - VP Finance and Operations Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The IT Project Manager III serves as a facilitator for projects led by the Office of Information Technology (OIT) and provides guidance to IT operational managers and project teams across campus. Focuses on best practices for project management on both departmental and enterprise-wide IT projects. Manages larger, more complex, critical IT projects requiring advanced knowledge and demonstrated expertise in project management. Oversees, creates, and implements project plans. Provides feedback and mentorship for other OIT project managers. Additional Department Summary: The University of Alabama is embarking to transition its on-premises finance and HCM ERP systems to a modern cloud platform. This position is a senior-level IT Project Manager responsible for serving as a liaison and mentor to operational managers and project teams. The IT Project Manager III leads more complex projects that require advanced expertise and a proven track record in project management. This position is time-limited to the duration of the project due to additional department staffing needs while engaged in this project, but could lead to regular employment at the University. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree and two (2) years of IT project management experience; OR bachelor's degree and four (4) years of IT project management experience; OR associate's degree and six (6) years of IT experience to include four (4) years of IT project management; OR High school diploma or GED and eight (8) years of IT experience to include four (4) years of IT project management. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education. CAPM or PMP certification. Demonstrated formal project management training. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) af074264 Last Name (required) 511ee787 Email (required) 44fc0eb3 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 89280213 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Systems/Technology Support Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) efb3cb09 Last Name (required) afa821b4 Email (required) 5aa8036a Friend's Information 609340b4 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 0a17043d Last Name (required) 750a49cc Email (required) 0398c29d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive con