    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/safestate-environmental-health-and-safety-consultant-ii-530669-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "SafeState Environmental Health and Safety Consultant II",
      "description": "SafeState Environmental Health and Safety Consultant II - 530669 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode SafeState Environmental Health and Safety Consultant II - 530669 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search SafeState Environmental Health and Safety Consultant II - 530669 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Health Care / Social Services Police/Security/Safety Closing at: Oct 6 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $62,300 - Midpoint: $81,000 (Salaried E10) Department/Organization: 214153 - Environmental Programs Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some overnight and weekend travel. Job Summary: The SafeState Environmental Health and Safety Consultant II provides complex industrial hygiene and occupational safety consultation services, including onsite visits to businesses and industries in Alabama. Additional Department Summary: Collaborates with management to provide appropriate environmental health and safety consultation and education services to new and existing clients. Works independently in developing and producing appropriate programs and services. Meets revenue targets for environmental consultation services. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in engineering, safety science, business, management, public health, or physical sciences and four (4) years of occupational safety experience; OR masters degree or higher in engineering, safety science, industrial management, public health, or physical sciences and two (2) years of occupational safety experience. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Strong organizational, communication and public relations skills. Knowledge of Environmental Protection Agency, Occupational Safety and Health Administration, and US Department of Housing and Urban Development regulations. Knowledge of EHS sampling techniques and equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree and two (2) years of experience in management of environmental assessment/remediation projects, management of a business in the environmental, safety, and/or health fields, management of environmental or occupationally related accreditation / certification programs, or consulting, designing, or implementing environmental management systems; OR bachelor's degree and four (4) years of experience in management of environmental assessment/remediation projects, management of a business in the environmental, safety, and/or health fields, management of environmental or occupationally related accreditation/certification programs, or consulting, designing, or implementing environmental management systems. The following is preferred prior to starting in the position, but at a minimum must be obtained within 12 months of appointment: 1) Federal and state accredited AHERA Inspector (reference 40 CFR 763); 2) Federal or state certification as Lead Inspector/Risk Assessor (ref. 40 CFR 745). Certified or eligible for certification as a CIH by the American Board of Industrial Hygiene. Certified Instructional Trainer (CIT), or Certified Hazardous Materials Manager (CHMM). Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) cb9a3994 Last Name (required) 392b888d Email (required) 9e3888c1 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 0cadb993 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health Care / Social Services Police/Security/Safety Health Care / Social Services Police/Security/Safety Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 09aaee51 Last Name (required) 1a5e7cfd Email (required) e4038011 Friend's Information be044063 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days.