    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/marketing-coordinator-ii-530644-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Marketing Coordinator II",
      "description": "Marketing Coordinator II - 530644 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Marketing Coordinator II - 530644 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Marketing Coordinator II - 530644 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Communication Marketing/Event Planning Closing at: Oct 5 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $48,600 - Midpoint: $60,800 (Salaried E7) Department/Organization: 206113 - Culverhouse Communications Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Marketing Coordinator II oversees marketing, promotion, and publicity functions for a college, division, or the University. Creates and implements marketing strategies using advertising, media, direct mail, etc. Coordinates production of materials specified in marketing plans and calendars. Consults with product and/or program development. Additional Department Summary: Leads communications and marketing work for the Alabama Entrepreneurship Institute (AEI) and The EDGE, Tuscaloosa's premier incubator and accelerator. AEI is part of The University of Alabama’s Culverhouse College of Business and serves the entire UA community. Supports the Culverhouse College of Business Office of Marketing and Communications. Contributes to college-wide marketing campaign execution and content development for the College and its associated units, functioning as an integrated member of the broader Culverhouse marketing ecosystem while maintaining AEI and The EDGE as the primary area of responsibility. Helps to lead the development and ensure the successful ongoing delivery of strategic marketing actions that include digital advertising, organic and paid social media campaigns, website content, newsletters, press releases, and other communications materials. Designs or oversees the production of marketing materials in accordance with UA and Culverhouse brand guidelines. Originates media campaigns tied to AEI programs and events. Supports the AEI Executive Director with communications needs. Supports the rollout of new initiatives, including membership programs, fundraising campaigns, and other high-level AEI priorities. Supports AEI leadership and colleagues with communications to AEI and EDGE advisory boards, partnering organizations, EDGE tenants, and other groups. Develops and executes marketing strategies to promote AEI and EDGE events, including social media promotion, email communications, digital and print collateral, and post-event publicity. Coordinates with AEI program staff and Culverhouse marketing and communications teams to ensure event marketing is timely, on-brand, and reaches the right audiences. Must be available to work occasional weekends and evenings in support of events. Helps supervise student employees and interns who support departmental communications, marketing, and outreach efforts, including task assignment and marketing relation performance oversight. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of marketing, public relations, communications, or advertising experience; OR master's degree and some marketing, public relations, communications, or advertising experience. Skills and Knowledge: Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to produce and manage a high volume of marketing content across multiple channels and audiences. Strong marketing strategy competency. Ability to develop and execute campaigns across digital, social, and print platforms. Ability to work effectively within a dual reporting structure and collaborate across teams. Strong interpersonal skills and professional judgment. Proficiency in design tools such as Adobe InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop, or Canva. Ability to produce polished presentations and branded marketing materials in accordance with UA and Culverhouse guidelines. Familiarity with content management systems, particularly WordPress or similar platforms. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in communications, public relations, marketing, or advertising and five (5) years of related experience; OR master's degree in communications, public relations, marketing, or advertising and three (3) years related experience. Experience starting up and/or running a marketing department for an organization. Experience with social media management tools, email marketing platforms, and digital advertising. Experience with project management tools such as Basecamp, Asana, or similar platforms. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 7e5aca80 Last Name (required) f40aa452 Email (required) f7d8dcf2 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. e0fd63c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Communication Marketing/Event Planning Communication Marketing/Event Planning Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 0f59c9a0 Last Name (required) 91ed2245 Email (required) f4f66852 Friend's Information 8df57c67 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) f916240e Last Name (required) 4bcfe8a0 Email (required) 9e976ad0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"
